            "review_title": "Review at Hồi Ký Mì Gia",
            "review_text": "clark\nForks of Salmon, California2 contributions\n0\nfor me , it's an okay\nApr 2026 • Solo\nhis place has a pretty big menu — almost 1cm thick — so there are lots of options to choose from. I went with the roast duck noodles for 59k, and the restaurant itself felt fairly spacious, with several 4-seat tables and a couple of bigger tables too. Staff were fast, friendly, and service was smooth, which gave a good first impression.\n\nThe duck nooldes was decent and only had 2 small bones, so that part was fine. But the main issue for me was the seasoning. The dish was just too salty, and it ended up covering most of the other flavors. That was a bit disappointing.\nRead more\nWritten April 22, 2026",
